{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"53d14cd03ec221ea","name":"card_event_buzz_bomb","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/BloodIron/events/card_event_buzz_bomb","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BUZZ BOMB","text":"Deal 1 damage to an enemy. Draw a card if it is the HQ.","flavorText":"The German \"Buzz Bomb,\" officially known as the V-1 flying bomb, was an early cruise missile and one of the world’s first guided weapons, used by Germany during World War II. It was developed as part of Hitler's \"vengeance weapons\" program to retaliate against Allied bombings. Launched primarily from sites in northern France and Belgium due to its limited range, the V-1 targeted London and other cities in southeast England, causing significant destruction and civilian casualties. The V-1 earned the nickname \"Buzz Bomb\" or \"Doodlebug\" because of the loud, distinctive buzzing noise made by its jet engine. This sound struck fear into the population below, as the buzzing would suddenly stop just before the bomb descended and exploded. In total, over 9,000 V-1 bombs were launched, causing thousands of casualties and leaving a lasting mark on the cities they targeted. The V-1’s development marked a significant step in the evolution of modern missile technology.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_buzz_bomb","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_buzz_bomb_title","SourceString":"BUZZ BOMB","LocalizedString":"BUZZ BOMB"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_buzz_bomb_text","SourceString":"Deal 1 damage to an enemy. Draw a card if it is the HQ.","LocalizedString":"Deal 1 damage to an enemy. Draw a card if it is the HQ."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_buzz_bomb_history","SourceString":"The German \"Buzz Bomb,\" officially known as the V-1 flying bomb, was an early cruise missile and one of the world’s first guided weapons, used by Germany during World War II. It was developed as part of Hitler's \"vengeance weapons\" program to retaliate against Allied bombings. Launched primarily from sites in northern France and Belgium due to its limited range, the V-1 targeted London and other cities in southeast England, causing significant destruction and civilian casualties. The V-1 earned the nickname \"Buzz Bomb\" or \"Doodlebug\" because of the loud, distinctive buzzing noise made by its jet engine. This sound struck fear into the population below, as the buzzing would suddenly stop just before the bomb descended and exploded. In total, over 9,000 V-1 bombs were launched, causing thousands of casualties and leaving a lasting mark on the cities they targeted. The V-1’s development marked a significant step in the evolution of modern missile technology.","LocalizedString":"The German \"Buzz Bomb,\" officially known as the V-1 flying bomb, was an early cruise missile and one of the world’s first guided weapons, used by Germany during World War II. It was developed as part of Hitler's \"vengeance weapons\" program to retaliate against Allied bombings. Launched primarily from sites in northern France and Belgium due to its limited range, the V-1 targeted London and other cities in southeast England, causing significant destruction and civilian casualties. The V-1 earned the nickname \"Buzz Bomb\" or \"Doodlebug\" because of the loud, distinctive buzzing noise made by its jet engine. This sound struck fear into the population below, as the buzzing would suddenly stop just before the bomb descended and exploded. In total, over 9,000 V-1 bombs were launched, causing thousands of casualties and leaving a lasting mark on the cities they targeted. The V-1’s development marked a significant step in the evolution of modern missile technology."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTar